WEBVTT

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>Soon after we met, we found ourselves alone...</i>

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.780
<i>I was in such a good mood that I carelessly overindulged in alcohol.</i>

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.740
Are you okay?

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.240
Do you feel better now?

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.290
I'm sorry... Shimao...

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.920
Rokka...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.710
You shouldn't stay in those dirty clothes.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.840
At least change.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.010
<i>In the sea of sleep,</i>

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.730
<i>I could feel his large, bony hands encircling me.</i>

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.190
<i>When I awoke, for some reason,</i>

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.190
<i>I was wrapped up my blankets.</i>

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.910
<i>Shimao was sleeping in the doorway, his shoes still on.</i>

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.700
<i>He had integrity, looked a little foolish,</i>

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.000
<i>and I became even more devoted to him.</i>

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.840
A dream about when I was young...

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.090
You're awake.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:16.970
Miho!

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:18.930
What are you...

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.600
You're still warm.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.230
Um, I...

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.060
Never mind. Just lie down.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.400
You collapsed, right?

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.980
You can't push yourself so hard.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.860
You're lucky Hazuki came by to check on you.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.530
H-Hazuki?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.740
Yeah. He's minding the store right now.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.500
Between the two of us, we'll cover the store for today,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.040
so you just get a good rest, Rokka.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:51.170
I'm sorry for putting you through all this trouble.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:52.630
It's nothing.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:08.310
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:14.480
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:21.030
I was prepared for the time you left

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:27.870
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:34.380
After I embraced you with all I had

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:43.930
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.600
filled my heart

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:54.110
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:02:54.110 --> 00:03:00.780
You gave me happiness

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.120
Until I meet you again one day

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.620
Until I know what you are truly like

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.160
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.840
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.960
I won't forget your smile

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.980
Would you move?

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.690
You're really getting in my way.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:38.690
If you and I were on equal footing,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.820
I'm sure Rokka would choose me!

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.580
You're a sore loser.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.740
I'm sure of it! Positive!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.080
How would we ever be on equal footing?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.290
Why not stop bitching and go on a quest for seven balls or something?

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.710
Fuck! God dammit!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.470
Can't even stamp your feet in frustration?

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.300
Whether I can or not has nothing to do with it!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.680
But you can't touch her.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.390
I'm number one even if I can't touch her!

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.270
Yeah, yeah...

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.940
Being with me is what will make her happy!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.190
She can't touch you, talk to you, or see you.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.820
You can't do anything.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.030
I'm gonna tell you something.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.080
It's not your fault the manager got sick,

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.700
but it is your fault that she can't move on.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.330
Let me have her already.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.760
I said you can't.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.050
Yes?

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.930
The manager woke up?

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:53.940
Yeah. I'm coming back down now, so you can go ahead and have lunch, Hazuki.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.900
Okay. Thank you.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.230
Uh-huh.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:58.360
Right.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.400
Don't go up there.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.780
Who put you in charge?

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.780
I won't let you go!

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.490
You can't stop me.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.530
Wait! That's no fair!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.790
Don't take advantage of her while she's weak.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.790
Look...

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.000
Don't!

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.540
Hey! Are you listening to me?!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.540
Nope.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.650
I'm sorry...

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.740
I'm sorry, Shimao...

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.210
Hello...

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:01.960
Can I come in?

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:20.230
If you don't look at me, I'm gonna scream.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.360
What? Don't.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.360
Then show me your face.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:38.120
You're looking a lot better.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:38.870
Good.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.340
Huh? Is your fever up again?

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.590
<i>Bony hands...</i>

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:56.100
<i>Large hands encircling me...</i>

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.450
Manager,

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.410
is your timing...

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.040
a little off?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.830
You're abrupt.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.250
I mean, I thought that the other night, too.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.170
Sorry.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.300
It's fine.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:34.100
I don't mind being the second choice all my life.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.180
Hazuki...

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.560
You're weird.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.190
<i>Without a body,</i>

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.190
<i>I can't even cry.</i>

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.700
<i>Why am I here?</i>

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.150
You might catch my cold.
<i>Why am I here?</i>

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.910
You might catch my cold.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.450
That's what I want.
<i>I can't go anywhere.</i>

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.780
<i>I'm neither here nor there...
Are you crazy?</i>

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:57.410
Then I won't catch it.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.580
<i>Who am I here for?
Then I won't catch it.</i>

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.250
<i>What am I here for?</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.040
Don't leave me alone!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.720
Earthquake?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.600
Looks like a big one...

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.820
What happened? Oh, no...

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.700
I'm worried about the shop.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.620
<i>A rapping sound?</i>

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.170
Hey...

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.710
Aren't you laying it on a bit thick?

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:55.630
This bedroom belongs to Rokka and me.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.140
Hazuki?

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.270
Manager, maybe we should check on Miho.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:04.810
Blood?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.150
Just a scratch.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.690
For now, let's go downstairs.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.110
Oh?

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.740
I think I dropped my phone.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:16.610
Huh?

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.450
I'll look for it, then come down.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.340
Leave.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:33.130
Please.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.300
If you don't,

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.390
I feel like

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.430
I'll end up killing you one of these days.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:53.230
That would actually put us on equal footing.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:10:01.080
But even if I disappear, another guy will show up in the manager's life.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.740
Are you gonna interfere every time?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.160
For how long?

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.670
Until the manager dies?

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.170
You do wanna rest in peace, don't you?

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:14.340
Eventually...

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.220
Well, speed it up.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.840
I'll help you.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.430
Really?

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.600
Yeah, if you actually will rest in peace.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.560
Okay, then...

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:33.480
Can I borrow your body once?

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.540
Oh, dear, Rokka. Is something wrong?

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.540
Um, what about the earthquake?

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.750
What are you talking about?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.540
You need to lie down.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.670
Huh? But before...

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.590
There wasn't any shaking.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:10:59.380
Really?

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:03.350
Come on, the store is fine, so go back to bed.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:04.810
Okay...

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:11.980
What are you saying?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.400
How would I even let you borrow my body?

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:15.150
It can be done.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.490
So lend me your body.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.360
And then you'll know.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.450
Like that's something I can just agree to!

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.700
Then I'll put a curse on you.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.950
Did I scare you?

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.000
Hazuki,

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:33.290
did you find your cell phone?

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.590
Yes.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.090
Anyway, how's the shop?

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:40.340
Looks like it's fine.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.090
Even with all the shaking.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.300
Oh, really?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.310
Manager, after your fever goes down,

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:49.480
would you teach Miho and me how to replenish the stock?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.060
Sure.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.980
Thank you.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.020
My shop can count on you.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:58.320
Sure. Get well.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.150
Hey.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.030
Hey, you said you'd help me.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.330
Lend me your body!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:09.830
I promise to return it.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:10.870
Sure you do.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:22.970
<i>I don't mind being the second choice all my life.</i>

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:37.690
<i>I miss him...</i>

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.210
I'm working.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.540
You have to work.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:56.960
Then get outta here.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.380
I'm supervising you in lieu of Rokka.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.880
I'm working hard, aren't I?

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.210
Hey.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.300
Think about what I said before.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.350
About what?

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:09.890
Your body.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:11.350
I can't lend it to you.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.600
All you have to do is go to sleep.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:13.270
I can't.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:14.690
Just for a little while.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.390
Forget it.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:16.560
Please!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.230
Not gonna happen.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:24.990
I don't believe it!

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.780
This... is a real earthquake, right?

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:38.210
Thank goodness! Somehow, we made it through the day.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.210
Yep.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.760
By the way, there was an earthquake today, right?

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.260
An earthquake?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.470
Was there an earthquake?

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.520
I hope Rokka gets better soon.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.480
This is the first time I've seen her down with a cold.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.730
It is unusual.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:03.400
Tough people don't notice the signs when they're starting to get sick,

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:04.860
which makes it all the scarier.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.740
Yeah. Good thing the shop's closed tomorrow.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.990
Yep.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.200
I bet you're hungry, huh?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:14.040
Yes. All of a sudden, I'm starving.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.450
I know, right?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.750
We almost never leave the shop together.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:18.750
How about grabbing a bite to eat?

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.500
Cool.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.170
Delicious.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.840
Sake really hits the spot, right?

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.050
Do you often drink with Rokka?

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.720
Once in a while...

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.970
Just at cheap pubs or restaurants while eating dinner...

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.350
I see...

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:39.230
Come to think of it, I wonder if Rokka is seeing anybody.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.360
What makes you ask?

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:45.230
Every now and again, my parents bring up the idea of setting her up with someone.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.780
Oh...

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.320
These days, it's not bad to have a son-in-law marry into the flower shop business.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:51.280
Well...

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:56.620
Of course, if the circumstances were right, I think closing the store down would be a possibility.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.330
But it's your younger brother's shop, right?

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.250
It would be an opportunity.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.750
If somebody doesn't give her a push...

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.920
We're talking about my brother after all.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.510
And I don't think she has much luck with men...

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:14.510
As her older sister-in-law, I worry about her.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.020
It may be that I'm just meddling...

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:23.940
But she's so reliable these days that I think we're dependent on her.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:30.820
I heard she was encouraged by her husband to throw away his belongings and get a divorce...

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:34.030
He could be oddly cold...

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:40.160
Ever since he was hospitalized for his illness during his elementary school days, he became philosophical somehow.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.040
<i>Philosophical?</i>

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:45.040
Apparently, he often wondered about what would happen after he died.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.050
<i>What part of that is the result of being philosophical?</i>

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.170
Anyway, that's why he was like that.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.010
Oh, yeah?

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.010
Uh-huh.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:02.480
Were you and your brother alike, Miho?

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.020
I don't know...

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.400
My parents doted on him.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:08.940
I figured.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:14.200
Well, I don't blame them, with him in a hospital bed all through childhood.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.490
Oh... I see.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.170
Come to think of it, I still have a photo on my phone.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:24.750
Wanna see?

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.840
It's an old photo.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.010
The three of us used to hang out a lot.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.550
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:33.930
There we go!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:37.510
This is from when we went to the Hanayashiki amusement park...

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.020
<i>Shit.</i>

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:50.530
<i>I think this is gonna make me depressed.</i>

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.200
<i>The manager is so damn cute.</i>

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:56.570
Are you okay?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.450
Um... Your eyes are similar.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.700
You think?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.290
I suppose there is a resemblance.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.460
About how many years ago was that?

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:08.590
I think six or seven years.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.590
Huh?

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.960
Miho, your phone sure has a long lifespan.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:14.470
No, I've changed phones, but this...

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:18.890
It's the last shot I took of my brother before he was hospitalized.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.680
I haven't deleted it, and carry it with me to this day.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.100
There's not much point in keeping it,

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:28.520
but it's not like you need to delete it either, right?

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:32.690
You shouldn't force yourself to pretend it's all right,

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:38.700
or try to forget when you loved him so much.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:43.330
Even if it's tough to face, you need to bury him.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.540
He is buried...

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:50.040
I'm not explaining it well...

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.880
Before, you told me that you don't like cut flowers, right, Miho?

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:54.340
Yeah.

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:57.760
Actually, more and more, I'm feeling the same way.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.340
Oh, imagine that.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:02.350
Cut flowers are kind of like ghosts.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:07.730
Normally, they bask in the sun and absorb nutrients from their roots, but when they are cut,

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:11.770
the ugly parts are discarded and only the beautiful parts remain.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:13.980
It's too selfish.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:18.160
I kind of get it and I kind of don't...

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:23.740
It'd be better if they were left to wither and become fertilizer for the next sapling!

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:37.800
<i>My hands can cultivate the earth.</i>

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:43.100
<i>They can plant trees and sow seeds.</i>

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.520
<i>They can even carry the manager.</i>

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:49.190
<i>But...</i>

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:52.900
<i>will I ever be able</i>

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:56.190
<i>to make her smile like that?</i>

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.890
Ow!

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.030
Morning.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:42.360
Is something wrong?

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.910
No. How's your cold?

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:46.830
Much better.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.450
I sweat a lot yesterday, so now I'm back on my feet.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.830
That's good to hear.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:53.920
Thank you.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:56.340
Please!

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:58.920
Won't you just faint for me?

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:01.170
All right? Like this...

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:05.430
Manager...

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:06.260
Yes?

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.430
Lend me your body!

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.890
Manager, you get the newspaper, right?

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.140
Come on, Hazuki!
Manager, you get the newspaper, right?

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:10.520
Come on, Hazuki!

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:11.640
Yeah, although I don't read much of it.

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.150
Come on, Hazuki!
Yeah, although I don't read much of it.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:13.560
Yeah, although I don't read much of it.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:14.400
Well, I don't really care about the paper.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.110
Hey!
Well, I don't really care about the paper.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:16.310
Well, I don't really care about the paper.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:17.150
Don't ignore me!
Well, I don't really care about the paper.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:17.690
Don't ignore me!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.400
How about going here on our next day off?

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:27.990
No Expiration Date
<b>Entrance Ticket</b>

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.080
The old newspaper subscription salesman gave them to me

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:31.960
so I thought we could...

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:38.590
Um...

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:43.090
Or we could invite Miho and all three of us can go.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.510
<i>I'm not good at gambling,</i>

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:53.140
<i>but it's either a dried flower or a potted flower.</i>

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.870
I'm sorry about this...

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.160
<i>I have only one wish.</i>

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.580
<i>I want her to keep smiling.</i>

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:26.260
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:32.020
you always smile

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:36.100
Tell me why

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:39.980
it won't go away

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.780
I gave you everything

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.610
You gave me everything

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:48.410
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.080
still my everything

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:53.290
I love you

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:56.670
The songs of midsummer days

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:59.790
are a fleeting miracle

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:05.760
like the winter snow

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:12.760
If I hadn't met you

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:15.980
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:23.480
and nothing would have pressed down on my dreams

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:29.160
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:36.200
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:41.330
When I close my eyes

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:45.340
you're right beside me
